        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/28: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-03T14:00:00+03:06">July 3, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 5—10:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. My 14, June 5, 1 p.m. Casoc’s cable 375 to San Francisco office raises
                    question of possible evacuation Dhahran. To protect insofar <pb facs="0590"
                        n="578" xml:id="pg578"/> as possible valuable concession rights the
                    Government should assume responsibility for evacuation by requesting company to
                    protect lives of Americans by temporary withdrawal from Saudi Arabia. The
                    Legation might transmit request to company representative here and should supply
                    copy to local government before evacuation begins.</p>
                <p>If desirable a skeleton crew inducted into military service could remain for
                    possible denial operations though evacuation would greatly increase threat of
                    interference from local officials.</p>
                <p>Circumstances necessitating evacuation might make impossible rapid communication
                    with Department or Minister Kirk and it is therefore respectfully suggested that
                    Department, company, and military officials formulate request together with
                    pertinent instructions leaving to discretion of Legation actual time of delivery
                    to company and local government. Legation is in constant touch with local
                    company representative.</p>
                <p>The foregoing is based on assumption that Army has no plan for taking over
                    defense and perhaps operation of Dhahran.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
